Fillets: three causes of segmentation faults in TKFillet (mitcad#122).

- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol (continuing a stripe from its previous surface
  data): when the face found past the contact point is an obstacle but does
  not hold the arc the contact left by (it lies across another edge at a
  vertex), StartSol returned false with c1obstacle set and HC a new, empty
  BRepAdaptor_Curve2d. PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine then took the obstacle
  branch and walked a surface/restriction blend on that empty curve
  (BRepBlend_SurfRstConstRad::Values). StartSol now leaves HC null and
  c1obstacle false there, so the caller ends or stops the stripe as for any
  other missing neighbour.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner and IntersectMoreCorner split the corner
  curve at the seam of the face at the end with Extrema_ExtCC; when the curve
  runs parallel to the seam, Extrema_ExtCC reports one distance but no
  points, and Points() read past the end of its sequence. The seam split is
  skipped for parallel curves (as ChFi3d_Builder_CnCrn.cxx already does).
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreSurfdata read the neighbour face index from
  the first stripe of the builder (myListStripe.First()) instead of the
  stripe at the vertex: with several contours that stripe may have fewer
  surface data, the out-of-range Value() left its sequence with a current
  index past its end, and a later Value() (ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter) followed
  a null node.

Test: geometry/tests/port/p0020-crash-fixes.cpp (ctest geometry.port.0020),
for two of the three faults. The corner curve parallel to the seam: a
chamfer and a rounding of 2 of the arc where a lug's top meets its bore's
wall, the lug ending or starting on the bore's seam (the prolongation of
the lug's end on the wall runs along the seam; the extrema in
PerformOneCorner's split of the prolongation are parallel): valid, the
blend's section turned through the lug's sweep within 1e-6; a segmentation
fault without the patch. A lug away from the seam, the boundary case,
builds the same with and without it. PerformMoreSurfdata's neighbour face:
the pipe and rod cut by an inclined end plane (test_fillet_overflow's
body), the junction rounded with 3 after another contour: after the other
junction (the first stripe's surface data at that index another blend's),
valid, the two adding what each adds alone, invalid without the patch;
after a box's edge in the same compound (the first stripe with one surface
data), valid, the junction's section between the end planes and the box
edge's loss within 1e-9, a segmentation fault without the patch. Each was
shown with TKFillet built without the patch, and without its
PerformMoreSurfdata change alone.

StartSol's obstacle without the arc has no test: no synthetic body reaches
it. A probe in that branch found no case in the geometry tests or in OCCT's
blend and chamfer DRAW groups.

